# ===== 114.44 Level VI, Advanced Mid to Advanced High =====
H('44.c.1.A',4,"At Level VI, speakers keep an appropriate tone while talking about past events, current events and future plans. The qualifier mostly consistent means the register is:","usually appropriate with occasional lapses",["never appropriate","always perfect","unrelated to the listener"],"Level VI register is mostly, not completely, consistent.")
H('44.c.1.A',4,"Which skill is expected of a Level VI speaker in conversation?","handling all time frames with a suitable register",["relying only on memorized phrases","speaking only about the present","answering only yes or no"],"Advanced conversation spans all time frames.")
H('44.c.1.B',4,"A student explains a scientific process and then a geographic trend in conversation. This shows ability to:","exchange information across varied topics",["recite one script","avoid abstract topics","use only greetings"],"Level VI handles geographic, scientific and other topics.")
H('44.c.1.B',4,"Which topic range fits Level VI verbal exchange?","geographic, scientific and cultural subjects",["only names and ages","only colors","only weather words"],"Advanced exchange spans many fields.")
H('44.c.1.C',4,"A formal letter with some elaboration, written across time frames, demonstrates:","writing with mostly consistent register",["a text message only","a shopping list","a single sentence"],"Elaborated correspondence shows advanced writing.")
H('44.c.1.C',4,"Which of these written items shows elaboration at Level VI?","a cover letter explaining background and goals",["a list of nouns","a short caption","a single word reply"],"Elaboration adds context and detail.")
H('44.c.1.D',4,"Producing written exchanges that provide information on varied topics with mostly consistent register means the writer:","adapts tone to the reader while informing",["uses the same slang for everyone","avoids detail","copies other texts"],"Written exchange fits the reader.")
H('44.c.1.D',4,"Which written exchange would meet the Level VI standard?","a formal email reply that informs a client with clear detail",["a one-word chat message","a list of random words","a doodle"],"Formal informative exchanges show advanced writing.")
H('44.c.2.A',4,"To appraise information from authentic print and electronic resources, a learner must:","evaluate its quality, purpose and perspective",["accept every claim","ignore the source","skim only the headline"],"Appraisal means evaluating.")
H('44.c.2.A',4,"Which of these is an authentic resource an advanced learner could appraise?","an editorial or an artwork review from the target culture",["a vocabulary flashcard","a worksheet with blanks","a sticker sheet"],"Authentic resources are made for speakers.")
H('44.c.2.B',4,"Appraising cultural practices and perspectives from authentic sources involves:","comparing, contrasting and judging significance",["copying quotes","skipping context","counting words"],"Appraisal adds judgment to comparison.")
H('44.c.2.B',4,"Why might two authentic sources appraise the same custom differently?","their authors hold different perspectives",["they use different fonts","they are the same length","they were printed on paper"],"Perspectives shape appraisal.")
H('44.c.2.C',4,"Listening to appraise an authentic broadcast means a learner:","evaluates the speaker's claims and tone",["only counts the words","ignores the content","mutes the audio"],"Appraisal requires evaluation.")
H('44.c.2.C',4,"Which source is suitable for appraising authentic audio?","a news interview made for native-speaking audiences",["a muted cartoon","a blank track","a printed list"],"Authentic audio is made for speakers.")
H('44.c.2.D',4,"An advanced learner compares how two documentaries portray the same tradition and judges which is more balanced. This is:","appraising cultural perspectives",["copying vocabulary","summarizing without thought","skipping the content"],"Appraisal includes judgment.")
H('44.c.2.D',4,"When appraising perspectives in audiovisual sources, a learner should look at:","who made the source and why",["only the length","only the volume","only the file type"],"Authorship and purpose matter.")
H('44.c.3.A',4,"A Level VI presenter plans, produces and presents a talk with mostly consistent ease and clarity. This shows:","strong presentational speaking",["silent reading","random speech","copying notes aloud"],"Presentations are planned and delivered clearly.")
H('44.c.3.A',4,"Which action best improves a spoken presentation's clarity?","organizing ideas and rehearsing delivery",["skipping preparation","reading a script fast","avoiding the audience"],"Planning and rehearsal improve clarity.")
H('44.c.3.B',4,"Planning and producing a written presentational communication with mostly consistent ease means the writer:","drafts and revises for clear expression",["writes without a plan","copies another paper","uses only fragments"],"Clear writing is revised.")
H('44.c.3.B',4,"Which written product is an advanced presentational communication?","a well-organized article on a social issue",["a list of nouns","a doodle","a text emoji"],"Articles present ideas to an audience.")

# ===== 114.45 Level VII, Advanced High to Superior =====
H('45.c.1.A',5,"A Level VII speaker engages in conversations with consistent register in all time frames. Consistent register means the speaker:","reliably adjusts tone to listener and setting",["changes tone at random","uses the same slang everywhere","avoids all formality"],"Consistency is the Level VII benchmark.")
H('45.c.1.A',5,"Which marks the difference between Level VI and Level VII conversation?","register that is consistent rather than mostly consistent",["shorter sentences","fewer topics","simpler vocabulary"],"Level VII is consistent.")
H('45.c.1.B',5,"Exchanging information on geographic, scientific, historical and cultural topics with consistent register requires:","wide vocabulary and precise tone control",["only common nouns","only gestures","only silence"],"Breadth and precision define Level VII.")
H('45.c.1.B',5,"A speaker moves from a casual talk to a formal debate about science policy while keeping appropriate tone. This is:","consistent register across contexts",["inconsistent register","lack of control","avoidance of topic"],"Register control across contexts.")
H('45.c.1.C',5,"Writing correspondence and reports with consistent register and elaboration shows:","sophisticated written control",["basic note-taking","copying","guessing"],"Elaboration with consistent register is advanced.")
H('45.c.1.C',5,"Which written product requires consistent register in all time frames?","a formal report describing past findings and future plans",["a list of nouns","a single sentence","a sticker label"],"Reports cover time frames.")
H('45.c.1.D',5,"Written exchanges that inform on a variety of topics with consistent register are expected to be:","clear, accurate and appropriate for the reader",["vague and casual","random and short","unrelated to the audience"],"Informative exchanges fit the reader.")
H('45.c.1.D',5,"Which written exchange best reflects Level VII?","a precise professional email that answers a complex inquiry",["a quick meme","a one-word reply","a scribble"],"Complex inquiries need precise replies.")
H('45.c.2.A',5,"To synthesize information from authentic print and electronic resources, a learner:","combines ideas from several sources into a new understanding",["copies one source","ignores differences","reads only titles"],"Synthesis integrates sources.")
H('45.c.2.A',5,"Which task is synthesis?","merging three articles' findings into a single argument",["underlining one sentence","copying a quote","counting pages"],"Synthesis creates a unified view.")
H('45.c.2.B',5,"Synthesizing cultural practices and perspectives means:","drawing connected conclusions from comparisons",["listing facts only","avoiding comparison","ignoring contrast"],"Synthesis builds conclusions.")
H('45.c.2.B',5,"A student explains how three sources' viewpoints on a tradition fit together. This is:","synthesizing cultural perspectives",["copying text","skimming","ignoring context"],"Synthesis weaves views together.")
H('45.c.2.C',5,"Listening to synthesize information from audio sources involves:","integrating points from several recordings",["listening to one clip only","ignoring content","muting the sound"],"Synthesis uses multiple sources.")
H('45.c.2.C',5,"Which task shows synthesis of audiovisual material?","combining a documentary, an interview and a podcast into one analysis",["watching a clip silently","copying credits","listing titles"],"Combining sources is synthesis.")
H('45.c.2.D',5,"Synthesizing cultural practices from authentic audiovisual resources leads a learner to:","form a unified view of how practices relate to perspectives",["memorize one clip","ignore the video","copy the subtitles"],"Synthesis connects practice and perspective.")
H('45.c.2.D',5,"Why synthesize rather than summarize a single source?","synthesis gives a broader, integrated understanding",["it is shorter","it ignores evidence","it avoids analysis"],"Synthesis integrates evidence.")
H('45.c.3.A',5,"A Level VII presenter plans and delivers a talk with consistent ease and clarity. This shows:","polished presentational speaking",["reading blindly","speaking off topic","avoiding eye contact"],"Consistent ease marks Level VII.")
H('45.c.3.A',5,"Which practice most strengthens a polished spoken presentation?","tailoring structure and language to the audience",["using identical slides for every audience","avoiding practice","speaking quickly"],"Audience awareness improves polish.")
H('45.c.3.B',5,"Producing a written presentational communication with consistent ease and clarity means:","drafting, revising and editing until precise",["writing once and submitting","copying","omitting structure"],"Precision comes from revision.")
H('45.c.3.B',5,"Which product reflects Level VII written presentation?","a cohesive essay with a thesis and evidence",["a list of words","a doodle","an emoji"],"Essays present complex ideas.")

# ===== 114.46 Seminar in Languages Other Than English =====
H('46.c.1.A',4,"In a seminar, a student drafts a researchable question with the instructor's guidance. A researchable question is one that:","can be investigated with evidence",["has no possible answer","is purely opinion","is unrelated to the topic"],"Research needs a question evidence can answer.")
H('46.c.1.A',4,"Which question is researchable?","How have social media changed communication in Spanish-speaking communities?",["What is the best color?","Why is it good?","Is it nice?"],"Researchable questions are specific and evidence-based.")
H('46.c.1.B',4,"Communicating with accuracy and fluency to participate fully in conversations means a student:","expresses ideas clearly and correctly in real time",["reads from notes only","speaks very slowly","avoids complex topics"],"Fluency and accuracy together.")
H('46.c.1.B',4,"Which scenario shows full participation in a seminar conversation?","building on others' points with accurate language",["staying silent","reciting memorized text","interrupting without listening"],"Full participation involves responding.")
H('46.c.1.C',4,"Comprehending language from within the cultural framework includes understanding:","nuance, subtlety and cultural references",["only literal word meanings","only spelling","only grammar tables"],"Cultural framework adds meaning.")
H('46.c.1.C',4,"Why does nuance matter when interpreting authentic speech?","tone and cultural context can change meaning",["words never change","only grammar matters","context is irrelevant"],"Nuance depends on culture.")
H('46.c.1.D',4,"Producing both formal and informal correspondence on varied topics requires the writer to:","choose style and register to fit the audience",["use one style for all","avoid greetings","write in fragments"],"Style matches reader.")
H('46.c.1.D',4,"Which pair shows formal and informal correspondence?","a letter to a university and a note to a friend",["two grocery lists","two math sheets","two maps"],"Correspondence varies by audience.")
H('46.c.1.E',4,"An in-depth research paper differs from a brief summary because it:","analyzes sources and develops a supported argument",["lists a few facts only","avoids sources","repeats one sentence"],"Research papers analyze and argue.")
H('46.c.1.E',4,"Which feature belongs in an in-depth report?","a thesis, evidence from several sources and a conclusion",["only a title","only pictures","only a list of words"],"Reports develop a thesis with evidence.")
H('46.c.1.F',4,"After completing research, a student poses new questions for further study. This shows:","reflection that leads to inquiry",["the end of learning","avoidance of the topic","lack of interest"],"Research opens new questions.")
H('46.c.1.F',4,"Which question follows from research findings about a language's regional variation?","How might regional variation affect communication in the workplace?",["What is two plus two?","Who won the match?","What is for lunch?"],"Follow-up questions build on findings.")
H('46.c.2.A',4,"A seminar student collects political cartoons, paintings and media clips for a project. This is:","gathering visual and media sources",["avoiding research","copying a classmate","writing without sources"],"Visual sources support research.")
H('46.c.2.A',4,"Why include visual images such as photographs in a research portfolio?","they offer evidence and perspective beyond text",["they replace all reading","they hide meaning","they have no value"],"Images provide evidence.")
H('46.c.2.B',4,"Compiling written ideas and representations means:","organizing notes, drafts and sources together",["discarding drafts","copying a book","avoiding notes"],"Compiling organizes work.")
H('46.c.2.B',4,"Which practice helps a student compile ideas for a project?","keeping dated notes and drafts in one organized place",["scattering notes","deleting sources","relying on memory only"],"Organization supports compiling.")
H('46.c.2.C',4,"To interpret information and draw conclusions from a wide range of sources, a student must:","weigh evidence from several viewpoints",["trust one source only","ignore conflicting data","avoid reading"],"Interpretation weighs evidence.")
H('46.c.2.C',4,"A conclusion is strongest when it is:","supported by evidence from multiple sources",["based on a guess","based on one headline","unrelated to the data"],"Conclusions need evidence.")
H('46.c.2.D',4,"Identifying bias in a news article involves noticing:","slanted wording or one-sided selection of facts",["the page number","the paper color","the font size"],"Bias appears in wording and selection.")
H('46.c.2.D',4,"Which indicates possible bias in a spoken report?","loaded words that push one point of view",["a balanced list of sources","citations to several viewpoints","neutral wording"],"Loaded language signals bias.")
H('46.c.2.E',4,"Using writing and speaking for reflection and exploration means the student:","thinks through ideas by writing and discussing",["avoids reflection","memorizes only","copies a text"],"Reflection builds understanding.")
H('46.c.2.E',4,"Which activity supports reflection?","keeping a learning journal about discoveries and questions",["skipping notes","avoiding discussion","copying a classmate"],"Journals encourage reflection.")
H('46.c.2.F',4,"Citing sources appropriately in a research project:","gives credit and lets readers verify information",["hides the source","is optional for all work","reduces credibility"],"Citations give credit and enable checking.")
H('46.c.2.F',4,"Which is an appropriate citation practice?","listing the author, title and source of every reference used",["omitting authors","citing only one of five sources","copying without credit"],"Complete citations credit sources.")
H('46.c.2.G',4,"A seminar portfolio is best described as:","a collection of work showing a student's learning and growth",["a single worksheet","a set of unrelated files","a grade report"],"Portfolios gather evidence of learning.")
H('46.c.2.G',4,"Presenting a portfolio requires the student to:","organize work and explain what it shows",["hand in blank pages","avoid explaining","read it silently"],"Presentation includes explanation.")
